 - `hyprctl switchxkblayout` changes the active layout index, not the stored names, so it never turns AGREE into DIFFER.
 
+## Operator decisions
+
+| situation | action | why |
+|---|---|---|
+| a keyboard prints `us` and empty names | delete the `kb_layout` line and reload; the default will compile | the fallback is what the dump prints after a bad name |
+| a pointer prints `-1.00` | put `scroll_factor` in the `input` block; the global option is clamped the same way | per-device blocks are optional sugar |
+| a `device` block matches nothing | rename it to the product name the kernel reports | the lookup compares loosely |
+
+Hyprland also recompiles every keyboard keymap on a hotplug and writes the compiled keymap back into the config
+store, so a hotplug repairs a bad `kb_layout` without a reload (Hyprland-InputManager.cpp:1180-1212, hotplug
+recompile).
+
 ## Limits
 
 - The XKB compile itself is not reproduced: whether a given layout/variant pair exists in xkeyboard-config is not checked; only the stored names are compared.
